{"title":"2024 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with 3 positive prime factors such that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/1/fd16fdd5d07a5419dc5f7c7259b43f4c5301f950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^n \\equiv k \\pmod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. For this to be true, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c63880ec8e95aeee56cc0f6f9fd26c318cdc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1 | n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> and similarly with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has to be squarefree, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428d854a61771c8934ab860702e28bf384524075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"11\" />. WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df42c4e11e90240b821f92593673803d0584ce02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; q &lt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. It is easy to see that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e129fbcb9c592946641c11f0c3eb03a078b4bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is one of the factors we have a contradiction. We can arrive at similar contradictions with pairs of factors such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c46d03a615e86881bb7509d8be42d3d37a4dfef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 7),(3,13), (3,19)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847df2e0624697b0d92ad958128d2fc277fa4075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. This eliminates most possibilities, so we can manually check triples now. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/0697dae65197058387a2c152caa32593e5e81e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5, 17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> does not work, and neither does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9530bb1b4bd4c06130304fd9d101018b0f01fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 7, 13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />. Finally, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824725646ef855be0b947dfc830c5daccd653553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 11, 17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> does indeed work, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdab182fe06f3eba1195bc840fc7d7f7985716b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 17 = \\boxed{561}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"172\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018030500\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 71/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3567/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31960:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018030500 and revision id 277021. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}